  "title": "Paula Y Probable NDE 6143",
  "date": "May 18, 2011",
  "content": "My experienced happened during my heart surgery. I had a double valve replacement and an aortic aneurysm repaired. I woke up with a very vivid memory that didn't feel like a dream. The experience is as follows: I was in a park and my deceased cat Amigo came running towards me and jumped into my arms. I recognized him instantly. I held him and hugged him. I was so happy to see him. I was smiling and extremely happy. He was happy to see me as well. He was rubbing his cheek against my face over and over. I kept squeezing him and feeling his fur. I was soooo happy to see him again. Then he jumped out of my arms and walked over to a park bench. There were people around, but no one stood out. I watched Amigo jump on to the park bench and curl up next to an old man. I realize the old man is my deceased grandfather. I start calling out to him; he looks over to me then motions with his hand for me to go away. He turned his head away and didn't make eye contact. I kept calling to him. My feelings hurt; he didn't want to say hi. I see Amigo sound asleep at his side. Then I was 'zapped', suddenly taken away from the situation.",
